>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `looper_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.looper_ss : string * (simpset -> tactic) -> ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates a simpset fragment containing one looper.

`looper_ss (name, mk)` is an anonymous fragment; adding it to a simpset
adds the looper as `add_looper (name, mk)` does.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val conj_ss = bool_ss ++ simpLib.looper_ss ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC);
>> SIMP_TAC conj_ss [] ([], “p ∧ q”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.SSFRAG`](#simpLib.SSFRAG).
